      <td class="content-column" id="content-area">
        <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
          <tr>
            <td class="title-area">
              <a class="title" href="/ant/2008/2-7/ant-v2-n7-p03-s.pdf">The
              moduli space of curves is rigid</a>

              <h3>Paul Hacking</h3>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>
              <div class="page-numbers">
                Vol. 2 (2008), No. 7, 809–818
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>
              <div class="paper-doi">
                DOI: <a href=
                "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/ant.2008.2.809">10.2140/ant.2008.2.809</a>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="article">
          <tr>
            <td class="article-area">
              <h5>Abstract</h5>
            </td>
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td class="article-area">
<p class="noindent">We prove that the moduli stack 
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><msub><mrow><mover accent="false" class="mml-overline"><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold-script">&#x2133;</mi></mrow><mo accent="true">&#x00AF;</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo class="MathClass-punc">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></math>
 of stable curves of genus 
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mi>g</mi></math>
 with 
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mi>n</mi></math>
 marked points is rigid, that is, has no infinitesimal deformations. This confirms the
 first case of a principle proposed by Kapranov. It can also be viewed as a version of
 Mostow rigidity for the mapping class group.
 </p>

</td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="article">
          <tr>
            <td class="article-area">
              <h5>Keywords</h5>

              <div class="keywords">
                moduli, curve, rigidity
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="article">
          <tr>
            <td class="article-area">
              <h5>Mathematical Subject Classification 2000</h5>

              <div class="keywords">
                Primary: 14H10
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="article">
          <tr>
